1
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:04,171
EPISODE 11

2
00:00:11,545 --> 00:00:13,780
Yun-hui, where are you going?

3
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:17,017
I have to borrow a tent for the market.

4
00:00:17,684 --> 00:00:19,720
By yourself? Want me to go with you?

5
00:00:19,786 --> 00:00:22,523
No, I'm fine. Why would you come?

6
00:00:22,589 --> 00:00:25,425
-Come on, let's go together.
-I told you, I'm fine.

7
00:00:25,492 --> 00:00:28,328
Come on, I'll go with you. Let's go.

8
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:29,997
There are no grasshoppers.

9
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:32,299
Still, just catch whatever's here.

10
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:38,705
Where did that punk Hyeok go, anyway?

11
00:00:38,772 --> 00:00:40,941
We must catch grasshoppers
for the market.

12
00:00:41,008 --> 00:00:42,776
We must get our instruments later.

13
00:00:42,843 --> 00:00:46,680
He's not answering his phone.
He's definitely sacked out somewhere.

14
00:00:46,747 --> 00:00:48,715
-I'm 100% sure.
-Guys!

15
00:00:48,782 --> 00:00:50,317
Hey, guys!

16
00:00:54,855 --> 00:00:57,491
Why are you making such a fuss again?

17
00:00:58,125 --> 00:01:00,027
I didn't come here to see you.

18
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,129
Sir.

19
00:01:02,195 --> 00:01:04,598
Anyway, where is my dear Kang Hyeok?

20
00:01:04,665 --> 00:01:08,569
I don't know.
He's probably holed up asleep. Why?

21
00:01:08,635 --> 00:01:10,103
You know what?

22
00:01:10,604 --> 00:01:12,673
You guys totally blew up!

23
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:14,942
Blew up? What did?

24
00:01:15,709 --> 00:01:17,077
Look at this!

25
00:01:20,681 --> 00:01:23,317
This must be love

26
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:27,220
EPIC CARP SLAP LOL, 1,030,025 VIEWS

27
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:29,022
SOYOU: WHAT'S BEHIND YOU?

28
00:01:29,089 --> 00:01:30,791
REDHOOD: SOMEONE ELSE CAME IN?

29
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:33,026
ANCKSUNAMUN: A CARP? WHAT IS THAT?

30
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:35,228
JUJUBETREE: MATILDA, BEHIND YOU!

31
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:38,599
JUJUBETREE: IT'S DAD! DAD SHOWED UP!

32
00:01:38,665 --> 00:01:39,800
Dad!

33
00:01:39,866 --> 00:01:44,438
EVENING: VIRAL HIT INCOMING
HANDEL: ISN'T THAT A CARP? LOL

34
00:01:44,504 --> 00:01:46,106
IKNOW: INSANE CARP SLAP LOL

35
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:51,645
Why is this going around online?

36
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:55,248
So embarrassing. What a total disgrace!

37
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:57,517
It has over a million views alone.

38
00:01:57,584 --> 00:02:01,188
It's on all kinds of websites,
plus popular forums and blogs.

39
00:02:01,254 --> 00:02:02,990
It's all over Twitter too.

40
00:02:03,056 --> 00:02:06,393
You guys are total stars now. Stars!

41
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,295
Please. Stars, my foot.

42
00:02:08,362 --> 00:02:10,297
This is nothing to be proud of!

43
00:02:10,364 --> 00:02:13,967
Still, it promoted Excellent Souls
big-time, right?

44
00:02:14,034 --> 00:02:15,335
Forget it!

45
00:02:15,402 --> 00:02:17,971
What punk recorded this
and put it online? Damn.

46
00:02:18,038 --> 00:02:22,242
Drop it. Don't worry about it.
We just need to catch grasshoppers.

47
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:24,077
Ki-jun, go see Mr. Hwang Man-gu.

48
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:26,279
-Borrow two more plastic bottles.
-Why?

49
00:02:26,346 --> 00:02:28,048
To sell grasshoppers at market,

50
00:02:28,115 --> 00:02:29,549
we need two more bottles.

51
00:02:29,616 --> 00:02:33,587
Fine! Stop making me do this stuff!

52
00:02:34,421 --> 00:02:35,422
Hey.

53
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:39,393
But will people in Seoul really buy
these grasshoppers and puffed beans?

54
00:02:39,459 --> 00:02:42,195
Of course, 100%! Aren't we from Seoul?

55
00:02:42,262 --> 00:02:44,131
Trust me, so go catch grasshoppers.

56
00:02:44,197 --> 00:02:45,999
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

57
00:02:46,066 --> 00:02:48,001
-There aren't any.
-I'll help too!

58
00:02:48,068 --> 00:02:50,404
Look deep in the rice. They're there.

59
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:52,439
Hey, where's Hwang Man-gu's place?

60
00:02:52,506 --> 00:02:53,573
No idea. Go, jeez.

61
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:55,375
No grasshoppers here. See any?

62
00:02:55,442 --> 00:02:57,411
Guys, I'm scared of grasshoppers.

63
00:02:57,477 --> 00:03:00,380
I'll go catch some over there.
There aren't any here.

64
00:03:00,447 --> 00:03:02,082
I caught one!

65
00:03:15,929 --> 00:03:17,698
How did you find me here again…

66
00:03:17,764 --> 00:03:20,200
You promised you'd give me more time.

67
00:03:20,267 --> 00:03:22,803
I'm not here to collect the money.

68
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:26,039
Look, I've got a question for you, see.

69
00:03:27,474 --> 00:03:29,076
What is it?

70
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:31,812
You're doing weekend farming here?

71
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:32,979
Yes.

72
00:03:33,613 --> 00:03:37,184
Coming out here, the air's real nice.

73
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:39,352
And I took a liking to this village.

74
00:03:39,419 --> 00:03:43,657
Plus, my kids are getting eczema
and struggling with obesity…

75
00:03:44,458 --> 00:03:47,094
Quit stuffing your face, you bastard!

76
00:03:47,794 --> 00:03:50,130
Hey, back to what I was saying.

77
00:03:50,197 --> 00:03:53,467
Yesterday, we planted
some lettuce seedlings here.

78
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:56,970
But when we came this morning,
the seedlings were all like this.

79
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,873
What on earth happened here?

80
00:04:03,443 --> 00:04:04,778
They don't even know.

81
00:04:04,845 --> 00:04:07,047
Farming out here isn't child's play.

82
00:04:07,114 --> 00:04:09,382
Water deer did this. Water deer.

83
00:04:09,449 --> 00:04:10,684
Water deer?

84
00:04:11,485 --> 00:04:14,988
-Hey, do they eat this stuff too?
-Water deer go crazy for this.

85
00:04:15,055 --> 00:04:18,525
We've suffered endlessly
because of water deer too.

86
00:04:19,226 --> 00:04:22,195
Since you have a wizard like me,
the God of Farming,

87
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:25,232
here by your side right now,

88
00:04:25,298 --> 00:04:26,933
well, there's a simple fix.

89
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,236
It's called cresol soap solution.

90
00:04:29,302 --> 00:04:31,772
If you plant that around this field,

91
00:04:31,838 --> 00:04:34,407
the water deer will go,
"Oh, my nose is rotting,"

92
00:04:34,474 --> 00:04:37,244
and won't even come near the field.

93
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:38,512
Cre-what? Hold on.

94
00:04:38,578 --> 00:04:40,413
Hey, write this down.

95
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:43,283
Stop stuffing your face
and write it down, bastard!

96
00:04:44,518 --> 00:04:48,121
-Cre-what?
-Uh, well, you see, it's cre…

97
00:04:49,256 --> 00:04:50,757
Never mind, never mind.

98
00:04:50,824 --> 00:04:52,959
I'll take care of everything for you.

99
00:04:53,026 --> 00:04:54,795
Just sit tight, okay?

100
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:57,030
That tone of yours just now…

101
00:04:57,097 --> 00:05:00,300
The way you talk to me is out of line.

102
00:05:00,367 --> 00:05:04,004
Did you forget where you and I stand?

103
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:06,473
To you, at least, I'm always the boss.

104
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:08,508
You little bastard, how dare you…

105
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:10,877
I'm very sorry.

106
00:05:21,721 --> 00:05:24,024
Where have I seen him before?

107
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:30,030
Uh, what if Bul-ja's here?
I can't run into her.

108
00:05:31,598 --> 00:05:33,133
Holy cow, you scared me!

109
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,068
Ma'am, you startled me.

110
00:05:35,135 --> 00:05:36,670
Never seen a face mask?

111
00:05:36,736 --> 00:05:39,573
What brings you here?
Oh, you came to see Bul-ja.

112
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:41,007
Bul-ja's not here.

113
00:05:41,675 --> 00:05:43,877
No, it's not like that.

114
00:05:43,944 --> 00:05:46,947
-I came to borrow plastic bottles.
-Oh, plastic bottles?

115
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:48,815
Check the shed. They'll be there.

116
00:05:48,882 --> 00:05:50,350
Okay, thank you.

117
00:05:50,417 --> 00:05:52,018
Please don't go out in that.

118
00:05:52,085 --> 00:05:55,655
It's my own home, that kid…
Just take the plastic bottles.

119
00:05:57,157 --> 00:05:59,492
She brings up Bul-ja every time.

120
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:03,730
Uh, where did she put those bottles?

121
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,235
Where are those bottles?

122
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,148
I'm back.

123
00:06:24,818 --> 00:06:26,086
What terrible timing!

124
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:31,157
Where do I hide?

125
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:33,360
Come on, seriously.

126
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:55,882
I thought only her face was pretty,
but her body's amazing…

127
00:06:55,949 --> 00:06:58,752
Han Ki-jun, what are you thinking?

128
00:06:58,818 --> 00:07:00,520
Shut your eyes, shut your eyes!

129
00:07:08,495 --> 00:07:15,468
YANGYANG TENTS

130
00:07:15,535 --> 00:07:17,771
Thank you for all your help.

131
00:07:21,408 --> 00:07:24,244
Yun-hui, I loaded everything.

132
00:07:24,311 --> 00:07:26,179
Okay, good job.

133
00:07:26,246 --> 00:07:27,814
Come on, let's go home.

134
00:07:27,881 --> 00:07:29,482
Yun-hui, Yun-hui.

135
00:07:29,549 --> 00:07:31,685
Can I please drive on the way back?

136
00:07:31,751 --> 00:07:33,620
You?

137
00:07:33,687 --> 00:07:36,323
No. How can I trust you to drive?

138
00:07:36,389 --> 00:07:37,757
No way, absolutely not.

139
00:07:37,824 --> 00:07:39,759
Come on, Yun-hui, please.

140
00:07:39,826 --> 00:07:41,828
You can teach me, Yun-hui. Please?

141
00:07:41,895 --> 00:07:44,331
I already told you no.

142
00:07:44,397 --> 00:07:47,267
Yun-hui, Yun-hui, please, please!

143
00:07:48,568 --> 00:07:50,070
Alright, fine.

144
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:52,005
But if you crash, it's all on you.

145
00:07:52,072 --> 00:07:53,606
-Got it?
-Yes, I got it.

146
00:08:00,113 --> 00:08:03,283
Hey! Don't just keep going straight!

147
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:06,086
Yun-hui, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

148
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:11,224
Okay, let's stay calm.
This really is our last chance.

149
00:08:11,291 --> 00:08:15,562
Seriously, if we miss this exit,
there's no way back to the village.

150
00:08:15,628 --> 00:08:18,798
There's a way back
if we exit by this overpass.

151
00:08:18,865 --> 00:08:21,001
This is really your last chance.

152
00:08:21,067 --> 00:08:24,170
Okay, don't panic. Blinker on.

153
00:08:24,237 --> 00:08:26,773
Don't panic. Blinker on.

154
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:29,809
That's it, good job. Still blinking?

155
00:08:29,876 --> 00:08:31,378
Wait for the right moment.

156
00:08:31,444 --> 00:08:33,513
Now just ease over to the right.

157
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,682
-Just ease right in, okay?
-Okay.

158
00:08:35,749 --> 00:08:39,786
Wait, wait, wait.

159
00:08:40,754 --> 00:08:42,389
Now!

160
00:08:45,158 --> 00:08:48,061
I can't! I can't!
Cars are coming too fast behind us!

161
00:08:48,128 --> 00:08:49,996
You took the overpass, you idiot!

162
00:08:55,001 --> 00:08:56,970
What a load of crap.

163
00:08:57,037 --> 00:08:59,973
Why did I go and say I like Americanos?

164
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,509
What is this, day after day?

165
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:05,545
Wait a second.

166
00:09:16,256 --> 00:09:18,358
Oh, that's not bad.

167
00:09:18,425 --> 00:09:20,126
My genius is just…

168
00:09:21,928 --> 00:09:24,831
Mister, can I please borrow your phone?

169
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:26,166
My phone? Why?

170
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:28,501
Just because! Hurry, please!

171
00:09:33,373 --> 00:09:34,541
Hello?

172
00:09:34,607 --> 00:09:37,077
Dad, it's me, Eun-u.

173
00:09:37,143 --> 00:09:39,712
The open class I mentioned
is tomorrow, remember?

174
00:09:39,779 --> 00:09:41,181
You can come, right?

175
00:09:41,848 --> 00:09:44,317
Don't worry, I didn't tell Mom.

176
00:09:44,384 --> 00:09:46,986
Okay, see you tomorrow then.

177
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:50,356
Mister, this is a secret from my mom.

178
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:52,592
Sure, all right, I got it.

179
00:10:08,141 --> 00:10:11,277
Don't ever think about driving again.

180
00:10:13,079 --> 00:10:17,016
Okay, I'm sorry.

181
00:10:19,986 --> 00:10:22,422
Oh! Look over there!

182
00:10:22,489 --> 00:10:25,592
Geez, what do you want me to look at?

183
00:10:42,442 --> 00:10:45,445
Wow, it's the ocean! Come quick!

184
00:10:45,512 --> 00:10:47,514
I told you, I don't want to go in!

185
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:49,182
No way, you have to come!

186
00:10:54,521 --> 00:10:57,724
Come on, I said I don't want to go in!

187
00:10:57,790 --> 00:11:01,261
At the beach, you just have to dive in!

188
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:04,197
I told you, I just want to walk.

189
00:11:04,264 --> 00:11:08,735
Still, thanks to me,
isn't it nice seeing the ocean?

190
00:11:08,801 --> 00:11:11,337
Unbelievable, you're so shameless.

191
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:13,806
Know how many years
you took off my life?

192
00:11:13,873 --> 00:11:16,676
I'm sorry. Don't be mad anymore.

193
00:11:19,379 --> 00:11:23,082
Gosh, it's still nice seeing the ocean.

194
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:27,053
I haven't seen the ocean in so long.

195
00:11:29,923 --> 00:11:32,158
You just smiled, right?

196
00:11:32,225 --> 00:11:36,262
You were frowning like this all day,
and now you're finally smiling.

197
00:11:37,463 --> 00:11:40,833
Wow, coming to the ocean was worth it!

198
00:11:53,613 --> 00:11:55,281
Looks like nobody's here.

199
00:11:55,348 --> 00:11:58,551
You don't think that guy
smashed our instruments, do you?

200
00:11:58,618 --> 00:12:01,087
Where did that jerk Ki-jun go?
What a coward.

201
00:12:01,154 --> 00:12:02,155
Enough, enough.

202
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:04,390
Let's grab it fast while he's gone.

203
00:12:04,457 --> 00:12:06,392
-Can't you just go alone?
-Say what?

204
00:12:06,459 --> 00:12:08,161
Cut the nonsense and come on.

205
00:12:26,646 --> 00:12:28,948
-There it is!
-Quick, let's grab it and go.

206
00:12:29,015 --> 00:12:31,517
Who knows what he'll do
if he catches us again.

207
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:32,919
You go first, go first.

208
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:38,258
I found it! I found it!

209
00:12:58,077 --> 00:13:00,013
-Isn't that a snake?
-A snake?

210
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:02,482
Uh, it looks like an eel.

211
00:13:36,582 --> 00:13:39,052
It's getting late. Let's get going.

212
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:45,992
Yun-hui, since we came to the beach,

213
00:13:46,059 --> 00:13:48,594
shouldn't we get some raw fish first?

214
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:49,529
Raw fish?

215
00:13:49,595 --> 00:13:53,366
I'm just hungry, Yun-hui.
Let's eat just one plate before we go.

216
00:13:53,433 --> 00:13:55,501
Forget about raw fish.

217
00:13:55,568 --> 00:13:57,637
Just go home and eat.

218
00:13:57,704 --> 00:14:00,139
Look at that!

219
00:14:00,206 --> 00:14:01,708
You're hungry too, right?

220
00:14:01,774 --> 00:14:03,276
Yun-hui, can we eat first?

221
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:05,011
Please, Yun-hui? Please?

222
00:14:06,045 --> 00:14:08,514
Then just one plate of raw fish.

223
00:14:08,581 --> 00:14:09,782
Deal!

224
00:14:13,953 --> 00:14:15,588
Gosh.

225
00:14:17,423 --> 00:14:20,493
Raw fish is best right by the beach.

226
00:14:21,194 --> 00:14:22,729
Say "ah."

227
00:14:23,496 --> 00:14:26,265
Forget it. I have hands too.

228
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,769
Don't leave me hanging.

229
00:14:29,836 --> 00:14:31,738
Say "ah." Come on, "ah."

230
00:14:31,804 --> 00:14:34,006
Ah, ah.

231
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:41,447
See? You're eating it just fine.

232
00:14:41,514 --> 00:14:44,917
Doesn't raw fish make you crave soju?

233
00:14:44,984 --> 00:14:46,386
Let's have just one glass.

234
00:14:46,452 --> 00:14:49,422
Are you crazy? What about driving?

235
00:14:49,489 --> 00:14:52,358
And I have to go
to Min-ho's school tomorrow. No, no.

236
00:14:52,425 --> 00:14:54,660
It's just one glass.

237
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:56,696
Please? Pretty please?

238
00:14:56,763 --> 00:14:58,431
Honestly.

239
00:14:58,498 --> 00:15:00,566
Then just one glass, mind you.

240
00:15:02,235 --> 00:15:03,903
Cheers!

241
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:11,611
Soju hits the spot with raw fish.

242
00:15:12,612 --> 00:15:15,648
So-fish, fish-so? So-fish, so-fish.

243
00:15:15,715 --> 00:15:18,584
But Yun-hui,
doesn't that leave you wanting more?

244
00:15:18,651 --> 00:15:21,721
Can we have just one more glass each?

245
00:15:21,788 --> 00:15:23,923
Now, now, I must say…

246
00:15:23,990 --> 00:15:26,859
I heard up to three glasses
won't even fail a DUI check.

247
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,208
We finished it already.

248
00:15:42,275 --> 00:15:44,377
We still have so much food left, too.

249
00:15:46,245 --> 00:15:47,880
Yun-hui.

250
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:51,684
Can we have just one more bottle?

251
00:15:51,751 --> 00:15:53,686
No, we can't.

252
00:15:53,753 --> 00:15:55,221
How will we drive?

253
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:57,523
Call a designated driver, like before.

254
00:15:57,590 --> 00:15:59,025
Come on, please?

255
00:15:59,091 --> 00:16:01,060
Gosh, honestly.

256
00:16:01,127 --> 00:16:02,895
Should we have one more bottle?

257
00:16:06,566 --> 00:16:08,501
Darn it.

258
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:12,004
We're home.

259
00:16:12,071 --> 00:16:13,940
Oh, you're back.

260
00:16:14,006 --> 00:16:15,675
What happened to your faces?

261
00:16:15,741 --> 00:16:17,210
We got hit with an eel.

262
00:16:17,276 --> 00:16:20,913
Yesterday, a carp slap.
Today, an eel slap.

263
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:24,717
Hey, at least we got hit
by a pricier fish than yesterday.

264
00:16:24,784 --> 00:16:28,921
-Doesn't it hurt a little less?
-Like hell it hurts less, you jerk!

265
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:32,158
Min-ho, why is your mom so late?

266
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,927
She isn't back yet?

267
00:16:35,695 --> 00:16:39,165
-What about Hyeok and Ki-jun?
-I don't know. They're not home yet.

268
00:16:51,377 --> 00:16:53,446
No, it's not true.

269
00:16:53,513 --> 00:16:55,147
It's not true!

270
00:16:58,651 --> 00:17:01,087
There's no way I like Bul-ja.

271
00:17:01,153 --> 00:17:02,622
There's no way I like her.

272
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,728
Still, that's such a relief.

273
00:17:09,328 --> 00:17:10,696
INCOMING CALL: AUNT

274
00:17:11,964 --> 00:17:15,501
-What is?
-You seem to be in a better mood.

275
00:17:16,736 --> 00:17:19,772
Because of Min-ho lately,
you kept frowning like this.

276
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:22,608
You were scowling the whole time.

277
00:17:23,643 --> 00:17:27,547
I couldn't stop worrying about you.

278
00:17:28,314 --> 00:17:29,582
Aren't I a good boy?

279
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:33,753
Yes, you're a good boy, a good boy.

280
00:17:35,254 --> 00:17:37,123
Then do this for me too.

281
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:40,493
-What are you doing?
-You did it for Min-gi before.

282
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,528
Please do it for me like that too.

283
00:17:44,864 --> 00:17:46,365
Oh, you.

284
00:17:46,432 --> 00:17:49,201
Yes, our Hyeok is such a good boy.

285
00:17:49,268 --> 00:17:51,604
Good job, good job.

286
00:17:51,671 --> 00:17:53,205
Happy now?

287
00:17:59,045 --> 00:18:02,481
So, I heard you're a medical student?

288
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:06,986
Doesn't your family say anything
about you doing this?

289
00:18:07,653 --> 00:18:09,288
Oh.

290
00:18:10,523 --> 00:18:12,692
My mother passed away.

291
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:16,862
I have a dad, but it's like I don't.

292
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:19,098
My dad and I don't get along.

293
00:18:20,032 --> 00:18:21,200
Why is that?

294
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:25,738
In my family, unless you're a doctor,
you're not treated like a human being.

295
00:18:25,805 --> 00:18:29,241
A black sheep like me is a disgrace.

296
00:18:31,077 --> 00:18:33,679
Oh, dear.

297
00:18:33,746 --> 00:18:36,515
But when did your mother pass away?

298
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:48,461
Eight years ago, due to depression,

299
00:18:49,729 --> 00:18:51,364
she overdosed on pills.

300
00:18:52,331 --> 00:18:54,066
Oh, my goodness.

301
00:18:54,567 --> 00:18:58,771
But I had no idea she was depressed.

302
00:19:00,239 --> 00:19:02,408
My mom…

303
00:19:03,376 --> 00:19:07,013
always acted strong too, just like you.

304
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:13,152
I was the only one in the world
who could protect my mom.

305
00:19:16,889 --> 00:19:18,824
I couldn't protect her.

306
00:19:27,933 --> 00:19:33,072
So I'll never make that mistake again.

307
00:19:36,242 --> 00:19:37,943
So you should…

308
00:19:39,545 --> 00:19:41,047
lean on me, too.

309
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:45,751
When you're struggling and exhausted,

310
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:49,021
please lean on me.

311
00:19:50,289 --> 00:19:52,525
I'll protect you.

312
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:57,029
Lean on me…

313
00:20:30,329 --> 00:20:33,032
-The phone is turned off…
-Her phone's off, too.

314
00:20:33,699 --> 00:20:35,968
What on earth happened to Yun-hui?

315
00:20:36,035 --> 00:20:38,804
I heard that kid Hyeok
didn't come home either.

316
00:20:39,438 --> 00:20:42,775
You don't think those two are together?

317
00:20:42,842 --> 00:20:44,110
That rotten jerk.

318
00:20:44,176 --> 00:20:45,911
Just wait till he gets back.

319
00:20:45,978 --> 00:20:49,048
Good job. A mom staying out all night.

320
00:20:53,119 --> 00:20:55,654
Hey, little rock star, off to school?

321
00:20:55,721 --> 00:20:57,089
Yes, Min-gi.

322
00:20:57,156 --> 00:21:00,726
Min-ho, I'll take you to school today.

323
00:21:01,293 --> 00:21:02,628
Let's go.

324
00:21:03,896 --> 00:21:08,300
By the way, what'll we do about
Min-ho's open class at school today?

325
00:21:08,367 --> 00:21:09,602
Huh?

326
00:21:11,036 --> 00:21:13,806
Seriously, where is this woman
and what's she doing?

327
00:21:38,531 --> 00:21:40,633
Why am I here?

328
00:21:45,437 --> 00:21:48,440
This is seriously driving me crazy.

329
00:21:50,276 --> 00:21:52,011
Eight o'clock?

330
00:21:52,611 --> 00:21:55,080
Hey! Wake up, wake up!

331
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:57,683
I said wake up!

332
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:02,087
Hurry and get up! Get up already!

333
00:22:04,824 --> 00:22:08,294
What? Did we really sleep here?

334
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:09,929
This is driving me nuts.

335
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:11,831
I told you we shouldn't drink.

336
00:22:11,897 --> 00:22:15,367
Whenever I get mixed up with you,
nothing goes right, nothing.

337
00:22:15,434 --> 00:22:18,771
Right! Min-ho's open class is today.

338
00:22:19,271 --> 00:22:21,740
This is seriously driving me crazy.

339
00:22:24,944 --> 00:22:27,046
Ow, my head.

340
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,915
I'm not sure I can even drive.

341
00:22:29,982 --> 00:22:32,451
You can't drive.
Give me the keys. I'll drive.

342
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:34,887
Forget it.
Trying to get us killed again?

343
00:22:34,954 --> 00:22:36,789
Don't worry. Buckle up tight.

344
00:22:36,856 --> 00:22:39,191
Hey! Leave me alone!

345
00:22:39,258 --> 00:22:41,093
-I'm a good driver.
-Trust me.

346
00:22:41,694 --> 00:22:43,929
How can I trust you again…

347
00:22:45,564 --> 00:22:48,133
-Darn it.
-Here we go.

348
00:23:00,512 --> 00:23:03,082
-What's this?
-Well…

349
00:23:03,148 --> 00:23:05,985
I guess I improved since you taught me.

350
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,455
Hold on tight!

351
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:27,139
If you embarrass me today,
I'm never going back to school, okay?

352
00:23:27,206 --> 00:23:28,974
All right, I got it.

353
00:23:29,041 --> 00:23:32,211
That's why I even got a perm again.

354
00:23:32,278 --> 00:23:34,780
Mom, you really can't come, okay?

355
00:23:36,282 --> 00:23:37,683
Okay, I won't go.

356
00:23:37,750 --> 00:23:40,119
Don't worry, and have a good day.

357
00:23:46,392 --> 00:23:47,593
Hurry up.

358
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,495
Go ahead.

359
00:23:52,498 --> 00:23:55,000
Min-guk, let's play together.

360
00:23:55,968 --> 00:23:57,569
My dad owns a company.

361
00:23:57,636 --> 00:24:00,272
He has so many workers and a huge car.

362
00:24:00,339 --> 00:24:03,142
Wow, really? That's totally awesome.

363
00:24:04,376 --> 00:24:06,478
Min-ho, what about your dad?

364
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:09,682
Min-ho doesn't have a dad.

365
00:24:10,683 --> 00:24:13,886
What? How can anyone not have a dad?

366
00:24:17,489 --> 00:24:19,124
The teacher's coming!

367
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:23,696
Attention, bow.

368
00:24:23,762 --> 00:24:25,631
Hello.

369
00:24:26,332 --> 00:24:28,067
Today is Dad's Open Class,

370
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:30,369
with dads as guest teachers, right?

371
00:24:30,436 --> 00:24:31,637
Yes.

372
00:24:31,704 --> 00:24:33,839
Listen well and pay close attention.

373
00:24:33,906 --> 00:24:34,873
Yes.

374
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:38,510
For our first class,
Min-guk's father will teach us.

375
00:24:39,411 --> 00:24:41,080
Please come in.

376
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:50,522
-He's a grandpa.
-Whoa.

377
00:24:52,992 --> 00:24:54,693
Hi there.

378
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:56,996
I'm Min-guk's dad.

379
00:24:57,663 --> 00:24:59,865
-Huh?
-Aren't you his grandpa?

380
00:24:59,932 --> 00:25:02,801
What I'm going to teach you all today

381
00:25:02,868 --> 00:25:06,271
is, uh, something you all love.

382
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:09,942
It's how to grow
sweet, delicious strawberries!

383
00:25:10,009 --> 00:25:11,610
Aw, man.

384
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:13,412
Shh, quiet.

385
00:25:16,048 --> 00:25:18,317
Strawberries, you see,

386
00:25:18,384 --> 00:25:20,352
prefer a cool climate,

387
00:25:20,419 --> 00:25:23,789
and are a perennial
fruit vegetable that…

388
00:25:29,395 --> 00:25:30,896
Please keep going.

389
00:25:30,963 --> 00:25:33,198
-What's wrong?
-What's with him?

390
00:25:35,534 --> 00:25:38,971
The seedlings are planted
after mid-September…

391
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:46,211
Come on, why'd you stop again?

392
00:25:47,246 --> 00:25:49,848
Is something wrong, sir?

393
00:25:51,050 --> 00:25:54,353
Um, excuse me, ma'am.

394
00:25:54,420 --> 00:25:56,088
I'm awfully sorry, but

395
00:25:56,588 --> 00:25:58,791
may I change the lesson topic?

396
00:25:59,391 --> 00:26:00,692
Yes, do as you please.

397
00:26:00,759 --> 00:26:02,561
Oh, thank you so much.

398
00:26:05,898 --> 00:26:07,232
Zdravstvuyte!

399
00:26:08,667 --> 00:26:10,769
Zdravstvuyte!

400
00:26:10,836 --> 00:26:13,005
Here's what that means.

401
00:26:13,072 --> 00:26:16,708
It means "hello" in Uzbekistan.

402
00:26:16,775 --> 00:26:18,177
Now, repeat after me.

403
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,578
Zdravstvuyte!

404
00:26:19,645 --> 00:26:21,113
Zdravstvuyte!

405
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:23,215
-It's fun, right?
-Yes!

406
00:26:23,282 --> 00:26:26,952
Want to hear it from a native speaker?

407
00:26:27,019 --> 00:26:28,053
Yes!

408
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:30,489
-Wait just a second.
-Okay.

409
00:26:32,524 --> 00:26:35,260
Honey, hurry up and come in.

410
00:26:35,961 --> 00:26:38,497
Come on, gosh, hurry!

411
00:26:41,934 --> 00:26:44,369
Come on, come inside. It's okay.

412
00:26:51,343 --> 00:26:55,114
Everyone, this is Min-guk's mom.

413
00:26:55,180 --> 00:26:56,448
She's pretty, right?

414
00:26:56,515 --> 00:26:57,716
Yes!

415
00:26:58,317 --> 00:27:02,020
Min-guk's mom is from Uzbekistan,

416
00:27:02,087 --> 00:27:04,957
so she speaks Uzbekistan's language
really well!

417
00:27:05,023 --> 00:27:07,292
Listen closely and repeat after her.

418
00:27:07,359 --> 00:27:09,094
Okay!

419
00:27:14,933 --> 00:27:16,468
Zdravstvuyte.

420
00:27:16,535 --> 00:27:18,003
Zdravstvuyte!

421
00:27:18,070 --> 00:27:20,472
Now, this time,

422
00:27:20,539 --> 00:27:24,543
"In Uzbekistan, does Kim Tae-hee
really plow the fields

423
00:27:24,610 --> 00:27:27,279
and does Song Hye-kyo herd sheep?"

424
00:27:27,346 --> 00:27:28,947
Want to hear a native say it?

425
00:27:29,014 --> 00:27:30,282
Yes!

426
00:27:30,349 --> 00:27:31,984
Hey, I'm so jealous of you.

427
00:27:32,050 --> 00:27:33,619
It's fun. Come on, do it.

428
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:40,792
In Uzbekistan, does Kim Tae-hee
really plow the fields

429
00:27:40,859 --> 00:27:43,195
and does Song Hye-kyo herd sheep?

430
00:27:43,262 --> 00:27:46,632
Then, Teacher,
how do you say "I love you"

431
00:27:46,698 --> 00:27:49,067
in the language of Uzbekistan?

432
00:27:49,134 --> 00:27:51,436
-I love you.
-Now, repeat after her.

433
00:27:51,503 --> 00:27:53,772
I love you!

434
00:27:53,839 --> 00:27:56,074
One more time, what was that?

435
00:27:56,141 --> 00:27:57,910
I love you!

436
00:27:57,976 --> 00:27:59,411
What did you say?

437
00:27:59,478 --> 00:28:02,114
-I love you!

438
00:28:13,759 --> 00:28:15,594
That's good. Really good.

439
00:28:15,661 --> 00:28:20,299
This makgeolli latte
is oddly addictive. So addictive.

440
00:28:32,744 --> 00:28:34,613
Hello? Who is this?

441
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:36,682
Um, this is Eun-u's father.

442
00:28:36,748 --> 00:28:39,351
Eun-u called from this number before…

443
00:28:39,418 --> 00:28:41,653
Oh, yes, hello.

444
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:43,555
Something urgent came up.

445
00:28:43,622 --> 00:28:45,557
I can't make it to Eun-u's school.

446
00:28:45,624 --> 00:28:48,126
Please be sure to tell Eun-u I'm sorry.

447
00:28:48,193 --> 00:28:50,128
Oh, yes, I understand.

448
00:28:50,195 --> 00:28:51,230
Thank you.

449
00:28:51,296 --> 00:28:52,698
I'll let you go, then.

450
00:28:52,764 --> 00:28:54,900
Oh, okay. Take care.

451
00:28:56,868 --> 00:29:00,305
Come on, he should've called sooner!

452
00:29:03,075 --> 00:29:04,810
Aw, crap!

453
00:29:09,281 --> 00:29:12,317
Everyone, did you enjoy
Min-guk's parents' class?

454
00:29:12,384 --> 00:29:13,785
Yes!

455
00:29:13,852 --> 00:29:16,955
Let's clap for Min-guk's mom and dad!

456
00:29:22,361 --> 00:29:26,431
Next up is Eun-u's dad,
but he hasn't arrived yet.

457
00:29:26,498 --> 00:29:29,301
Eun-u, your dad really said
he'd come today, right?

458
00:29:29,368 --> 00:29:32,304
Yes, he definitely promised he'd come.
He'll be here.

459
00:29:34,973 --> 00:29:35,907
Who are…

460
00:29:35,974 --> 00:29:39,311
I, um, got a call from Eun-u's dad.
Something urgent came up,

461
00:29:39,378 --> 00:29:41,380
so he says he can't make it.

462
00:29:41,446 --> 00:29:43,315
Oh, is that so?

463
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:48,353
Um, could I fill in for him instead?

464
00:29:48,420 --> 00:29:50,188
I'm basically like Eun-u's uncle.

465
00:29:50,255 --> 00:29:53,558
Oh, are you? Then I'm so relieved!

466
00:29:56,428 --> 00:30:00,465
Now, here's what I'll teach you today.

467
00:30:00,532 --> 00:30:03,702
Well, this is… Gosh, this is… man.

468
00:30:03,769 --> 00:30:05,003
Alright.

469
00:30:06,338 --> 00:30:09,274
It's how to open makgeolli
without it overflowing.

470
00:30:10,709 --> 00:30:12,878
Now, the thing about makgeolli is

471
00:30:12,944 --> 00:30:15,480
you have to shake it
and mix it to drink it.

472
00:30:15,547 --> 00:30:17,516
Shake it one way so it won't overflow.

473
00:30:17,582 --> 00:30:19,551
In one direction like this, see?

474
00:30:19,618 --> 00:30:21,186
Shake it this way, this way.

475
00:30:21,253 --> 00:30:23,755
Then twist the cap slightly, hiss.

476
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:25,524
Then squeeze its belly button.

477
00:30:25,590 --> 00:30:27,659
"Did you eat? Yes, I ate."

478
00:30:27,726 --> 00:30:30,362
Say hi, and twist the cap again, hiss.

479
00:30:30,429 --> 00:30:32,464
Then squeeze its belly button.

480
00:30:32,531 --> 00:30:36,601
Then you just pop the cap open
like this, and…

481
00:30:37,736 --> 00:30:40,572
gosh, this shouldn't be overflowing!

482
00:30:40,639 --> 00:30:42,841
It's because I ran here! I ran here!

483
00:30:42,908 --> 00:30:45,777
How this uncle pours makgeolli
without it overflowing,

484
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:47,746
how to store makgeolli,

485
00:30:47,813 --> 00:30:51,750
-and makgeolli…
-Makgeolli latte, makgeolli latte.

486
00:30:51,817 --> 00:30:55,554
Oh, yes, you even learned how to make
a makgeolli latte, right?

487
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:56,855
Yes.

488
00:30:56,922 --> 00:30:59,191
Next up is Min-ho's turn.

489
00:30:59,257 --> 00:31:01,793
Min-ho, your mom isn't here yet.

490
00:31:02,561 --> 00:31:04,196
Well…

491
00:31:05,664 --> 00:31:08,200
my mom says she's too busy to come.

492
00:31:08,266 --> 00:31:10,168
Oh, really?

493
00:31:10,235 --> 00:31:12,537
Then today's Dad's Open Class ends--

494
00:31:12,604 --> 00:31:15,507
Wait! Man, my heart is pounding!

495
00:31:16,508 --> 00:31:17,976
Min-ki!

496
00:31:18,043 --> 00:31:19,845
I'm, uh, Min-ho's uncle.

497
00:31:19,911 --> 00:31:22,914
Instead of Dad's Open Class,
is Uncle's Open Class okay?

498
00:31:22,981 --> 00:31:24,216
Excuse me?

499
00:31:24,282 --> 00:31:25,784
Oh, of course!

500
00:31:25,851 --> 00:31:27,686
Oh, really? Thank you so much!

501
00:31:33,158 --> 00:31:35,460
Kids, it's time for music class!

502
00:31:35,527 --> 00:31:37,028
And not just any…

503
00:31:39,097 --> 00:31:40,565
Rock and roll!

504
00:31:40,632 --> 00:31:43,535
Today, I'm inviting you
into the world of rock!

505
00:31:43,602 --> 00:31:44,870
Here we go!

506
00:31:48,039 --> 00:31:50,208
What are you doing? Get up, everyone!

507
00:31:51,143 --> 00:31:52,577
Hands up over your heads!

508
00:31:52,644 --> 00:31:55,714
Oh, yeah! Everybody rock and roll!

509
00:31:55,781 --> 00:31:58,183
Shake your heads like this, like this!

510
00:32:12,731 --> 00:32:14,933
What are you doing? You said to hurry.

511
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:17,302
Go on, hurry! Hurry up and go!

512
00:32:22,941 --> 00:32:24,176
Rock and roll!

513
00:32:43,061 --> 00:32:46,898
Come on, you have to
shake your head more like this!

514
00:32:53,138 --> 00:32:56,708
Eun-u, please listen to me!

515
00:32:57,576 --> 00:33:00,278
Min-guk, how did Mom and I do today?

516
00:33:00,345 --> 00:33:03,782
-We did great, right?
-Yes, the kids said it was really fun.

517
00:33:03,849 --> 00:33:07,319
-Mom, they said you're super pretty.
-Really?

518
00:33:07,385 --> 00:33:09,521
Then should we go into town today

519
00:33:09,588 --> 00:33:12,023
for your favorite pork ribs, Min-guk?

520
00:33:12,090 --> 00:33:14,125
Pork ribs?

521
00:33:14,192 --> 00:33:15,861
All right, let's go!

522
00:33:18,129 --> 00:33:19,698
Let's go!

523
00:33:25,203 --> 00:33:27,038
Where did you go yesterday?

524
00:33:27,105 --> 00:33:29,975
Well, um… one thing led to another,

525
00:33:30,041 --> 00:33:32,344
and I ended up going to the beach.

526
00:33:32,410 --> 00:33:35,280
Somehow, I wound up
having a drink, and well…

527
00:33:35,347 --> 00:33:38,316
Way to go. And you're a mom, really…

528
00:33:39,551 --> 00:33:41,253
I'm sorry.

529
00:33:42,420 --> 00:33:45,690
Min-ho, I'm so sorry.

530
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:49,060
No, it was super fun thanks to Min-gi.

531
00:33:49,127 --> 00:33:53,665
Mom, we're going on a picnic tomorrow.
Can't Min-gi come with us?

532
00:33:53,732 --> 00:33:55,100
Oh, how could we do that?

533
00:33:55,166 --> 00:33:57,769
-No, Min-gi's busy.
-Sure, I'll go with you.

534
00:33:57,836 --> 00:34:00,372
I've worked so hard,
so I can take a day off.

535
00:34:00,438 --> 00:34:02,507
-It's fine, it's fine.
-Really?

536
00:34:02,574 --> 00:34:04,743
Yay! Min-gi, you're the best!

537
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:05,777
High five!

538
00:34:05,844 --> 00:34:08,280
Yay! Min-gi, you're the best!

539
00:34:10,782 --> 00:34:12,384
Thanks.

540
00:34:12,450 --> 00:34:15,754
Oh, save it. It's no big deal.

541
00:34:16,521 --> 00:34:18,056
I mean it.

542
00:34:18,123 --> 00:34:20,091
Thank you, truly.

543
00:34:22,994 --> 00:34:25,430
Min-ho, let's go together!

544
00:34:28,967 --> 00:34:30,835
-You petty jerk.
-You scared me!

545
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:31,937
What's that about?

546
00:34:32,003 --> 00:34:34,739
Anyway, you're a real petty jerk, man.

547
00:34:39,844 --> 00:34:41,780
That guy, seriously…

548
00:34:48,286 --> 00:34:51,222
Hey, Yu-na, what's up?

549
00:34:51,289 --> 00:34:54,693
Nothing, you just crossed my mind.

550
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:57,295
-Is country life manageable?
-Of course.

551
00:34:57,362 --> 00:35:00,332
The cabbages are growing so fast now!

552
00:35:01,533 --> 00:35:03,034
That's good.

553
00:35:04,469 --> 00:35:07,539
Should I quit singing too

554
00:35:07,606 --> 00:35:09,941
and just go farm with you?

555
00:35:10,008 --> 00:35:11,676
What are you talking about now?

556
00:35:11,743 --> 00:35:13,411
It's just…

557
00:35:14,412 --> 00:35:17,649
-I'm worn out lately.
-You don't know how good you have it.

558
00:35:17,716 --> 00:35:20,485
Some of us are growing cabbages
to put out an album.

559
00:35:20,552 --> 00:35:22,887
You just wait right there.

560
00:35:22,954 --> 00:35:25,557
I'll catch right up to you soon.

561
00:35:26,458 --> 00:35:27,959
Okay, got it.

562
00:35:28,026 --> 00:35:30,328
I have a shoot, so I have to go.

563
00:36:00,058 --> 00:36:02,127
Why aren't you answering my calls?

564
00:36:02,193 --> 00:36:04,562
The CEO's going nuts
for me to bring you now.

565
00:36:05,230 --> 00:36:06,865
I told you I'd never go back.

566
00:36:06,931 --> 00:36:09,768
They're conglomerate heirs
you'd know just by name.

567
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:11,403
It can't hurt to impress them.

568
00:36:11,469 --> 00:36:14,406
You want me to go again
just to be treated like a toy?

569
00:36:14,472 --> 00:36:17,242
Plus, those guys even do drugs.
Do you know that?

570
00:36:17,308 --> 00:36:19,811
So just go and play along for a bit.

571
00:36:19,878 --> 00:36:21,346
Others are dying to go.

572
00:36:21,413 --> 00:36:23,314
Then take the ones dying to go.

573
00:36:23,948 --> 00:36:26,051
Hey, are you really doing this?

574
00:36:27,986 --> 00:36:29,387
Yu-na.

575
00:36:30,088 --> 00:36:32,524
I don't want to do this.

576
00:36:32,590 --> 00:36:35,794
But the CEO's losing it,
saying to bring you no matter what.

577
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:40,031
For my sake, please do this
just one more time today.

578
00:36:44,135 --> 00:36:47,005
I hate Dad! Dad is so mean!

579
00:36:48,273 --> 00:36:51,609
Well, your dad said he got
super busy all of a sudden.

580
00:36:51,676 --> 00:36:53,545
He felt really sorry about it.

581
00:36:53,611 --> 00:36:56,881
So don't hate Dad too much, okay?

582
00:36:56,948 --> 00:37:00,251
There, there, stop crying now.

583
00:37:00,318 --> 00:37:02,187
What are you talking about?

584
00:37:02,854 --> 00:37:05,490
-Mi-yeong.
-What do you mean, her dad?

585
00:37:06,057 --> 00:37:08,626
Eun-u, you didn't call Dad, did you?

586
00:37:11,129 --> 00:37:13,798
Um, it's not Eun-u's fault.

587
00:37:13,865 --> 00:37:16,367
I'm the one who called him.

588
00:37:16,434 --> 00:37:19,137
I heard her school was having
a dads' open class.

589
00:37:19,204 --> 00:37:20,572
What?

590
00:37:20,638 --> 00:37:24,442
Who on earth are you to do that?
Who do you think you are?

591
00:37:24,509 --> 00:37:26,911
-I'm sorry.
-Does "sorry" fix everything?

592
00:37:26,978 --> 00:37:30,582
She's too young to know better.
At least you should've stopped her.

593
00:37:30,648 --> 00:37:32,951
Right, I didn't think it through.

594
00:37:33,017 --> 00:37:34,452
I'm really sorry.

595
00:37:34,519 --> 00:37:35,854
I'll get going now.

596
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:37,655
Eun-u, I'll be going now.

597
00:37:37,722 --> 00:37:39,624
Don't make her cry.

598
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:50,335
Oh, it's warm. Oh, so warm.

599
00:37:51,069 --> 00:37:53,271
Oh, that feels good. So good.

600
00:37:59,043 --> 00:38:00,311
Thanks.

601
00:38:04,249 --> 00:38:05,650
Um…

602
00:38:06,217 --> 00:38:08,920
thank you so much for today.

603
00:38:08,987 --> 00:38:12,991
It's no big deal.
As long as Min-ho liked it.

604
00:38:13,758 --> 00:38:15,460
You're right.

605
00:38:15,527 --> 00:38:19,030
I don't know how long it's been
since Min-ho smiled so brightly.

606
00:38:19,097 --> 00:38:21,900
It's been a long time
since I saw you smile, too.

607
00:38:21,966 --> 00:38:25,336
So stop frowning and smile more often.

608
00:38:27,839 --> 00:38:29,340
Um…

609
00:38:29,407 --> 00:38:31,709
can I ask you something?

610
00:38:31,776 --> 00:38:33,211
What?

611
00:38:33,278 --> 00:38:36,648
I'm grateful
you're so good to Min-ho and me,

612
00:38:37,916 --> 00:38:39,751
but what feelings are behind it?

613
00:38:41,386 --> 00:38:42,987
What feelings?

614
00:38:47,826 --> 00:38:50,128
When you look upset,

615
00:38:51,229 --> 00:38:52,764
it bothers me too.

616
00:38:53,431 --> 00:38:54,999
When you cry,

617
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:57,001
I feel sad too.

618
00:38:57,068 --> 00:39:00,705
And when you smile, I feel good too.

619
00:39:02,707 --> 00:39:04,375
I want you to be happy.

620
00:39:05,910 --> 00:39:07,679
After all, you're my first love.

621
00:39:07,745 --> 00:39:10,148
I have to provide warranty service.

622
00:39:12,283 --> 00:39:14,719
It's cold. I'm going. Good night.

623
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:18,056
Okay, good night.

624
00:39:39,143 --> 00:39:42,480
Mi-yeong,
what brings you here at this hour?

625
00:39:53,458 --> 00:39:56,661
I'm sorry about earlier.

626
00:39:56,728 --> 00:39:58,096
Don't be.

627
00:39:58,663 --> 00:40:02,000
I overstepped. It's all my fault.

628
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:03,868
No, I was too harsh.

629
00:40:03,935 --> 00:40:07,071
It's okay. I understand how you feel.

630
00:40:08,339 --> 00:40:10,074
Pour me a drink too.

631
00:40:10,141 --> 00:40:11,409
Sure.

632
00:40:25,256 --> 00:40:29,227
I spent my whole marriage
overwhelmed by constant fighting.

633
00:40:30,161 --> 00:40:32,297
He had so many other women.

634
00:40:33,998 --> 00:40:37,635
From the moment we married
until the day we divorced,

635
00:40:37,702 --> 00:40:40,772
I lived like that the whole time.

636
00:40:41,706 --> 00:40:43,775
For Eun-u's sake,

637
00:40:45,810 --> 00:40:50,114
I endured it again and again,

638
00:40:51,349 --> 00:40:53,651
and kept holding on,

639
00:40:54,719 --> 00:40:56,888
but I just couldn't take it anymore.

640
00:40:59,958 --> 00:41:04,595
When I asked for a divorce,
he eagerly threw me alimony and signed.

641
00:41:07,532 --> 00:41:09,000
This is all…

642
00:41:11,102 --> 00:41:13,805
my punishment for abandoning you.

643
00:41:14,405 --> 00:41:17,041
Don't talk like that.

644
00:41:21,379 --> 00:41:24,515
Why is my life like this, seriously?

645
00:41:27,385 --> 00:41:28,686
Don't cry.

646
00:41:29,821 --> 00:41:31,022
Oh, dear.

647
00:41:31,656 --> 00:41:33,324
Oh, no.

648
00:41:41,432 --> 00:41:43,401
Sang-deuk.

649
00:41:46,537 --> 00:41:48,706
-Stop crying.
-Sang-deuk.

650
00:41:53,644 --> 00:41:55,179
Stop crying.

651
00:41:56,180 --> 00:41:58,416
It's all in the past now.

652
00:42:25,877 --> 00:42:28,012
I don't know…

653
00:42:42,860 --> 00:42:45,997
Gosh, why am I so sleepy this morning?

654
00:42:46,064 --> 00:42:48,266
Guess I should just take a nap.

655
00:42:59,777 --> 00:43:01,979
Gosh, I can barely keep my eyes open.

656
00:43:02,613 --> 00:43:05,283
Gosh, why is this place such a mess?

657
00:43:05,850 --> 00:43:08,186
Which jerk ate and didn't clean up?

658
00:43:08,252 --> 00:43:10,988
What crazy bastard left one sock here?

659
00:43:11,055 --> 00:43:14,025
Gosh, they're out of their minds.

660
00:43:15,259 --> 00:43:16,694
Ugh.

661
00:43:27,004 --> 00:43:29,040
Hey, Ki-jun, have some.

662
00:43:30,508 --> 00:43:32,610
Hey!

663
00:43:33,277 --> 00:43:34,779
-Ki-jun!
-Huh?

664
00:43:35,346 --> 00:43:37,748
What's with you? You look spaced out.

665
00:43:37,815 --> 00:43:39,417
I told you, it's nothing.

666
00:43:39,484 --> 00:43:41,652
Is there a law against spacing out?

667
00:43:41,719 --> 00:43:45,022
If it's nothing, fine.
Why get so mad, you punk?

668
00:43:45,089 --> 00:43:47,325
Because you keep saying weird things.

669
00:43:50,194 --> 00:43:53,431
Conglomerate heirs smoking marijuana
at a location in Seoul

670
00:43:53,498 --> 00:43:55,366
were caught by the police.

671
00:43:55,433 --> 00:43:59,103
And popular singer Yu-na
was reportedly at the scene…

672
00:43:59,170 --> 00:44:00,771
Hey, hey, look at this!

673
00:44:02,006 --> 00:44:05,009
However, she tested negative,

674
00:44:05,076 --> 00:44:06,944
so she was sent home at dawn.

675
00:44:07,011 --> 00:44:11,482
Still, this is expected
to deal a huge blow to her image.

676
00:44:16,621 --> 00:44:18,923
Sorry, I don't think I can go today.

677
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:31,002
Don't those jerks ever sleep?

678
00:44:31,068 --> 00:44:33,671
Just camped right outside our agency.

679
00:44:33,738 --> 00:44:35,973
All her event bookings are canceled.

680
00:44:36,040 --> 00:44:39,710
Advertisers are in an uproar,
threatening breach-of-contract suits.

681
00:44:39,777 --> 00:44:42,847
-What should we do, CEO?
-We really stepped in shit.

682
00:44:42,914 --> 00:44:45,449
Why'd she get mixed up with marijuana?

683
00:44:46,217 --> 00:44:47,785
Where are you going?

684
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:49,487
The restroom.

685
00:44:59,030 --> 00:45:00,665
Min-gi.

686
00:45:02,033 --> 00:45:03,367
Follow me.

687
00:45:06,771 --> 00:45:09,407
Where on earth did Min-gi go?

688
00:45:10,608 --> 00:45:12,343
Did he go see Yu-na?

689
00:45:12,410 --> 00:45:15,680
No way. What could he do if he went…

690
00:45:15,746 --> 00:45:19,917
By the way, do you know
that young singer on the news earlier?

691
00:45:19,984 --> 00:45:22,119
Yes, we used to be trainees together.

692
00:45:22,186 --> 00:45:24,055
Oh, really?

693
00:45:24,121 --> 00:45:27,592
Right, didn't you guys say
you used to be singers?

694
00:45:27,658 --> 00:45:30,194
Yes, though we totally flopped.

695
00:45:32,763 --> 00:45:34,398
So what have you been doing?

696
00:45:34,465 --> 00:45:37,034
Tomorrow is Sang-eun's birthday.

697
00:45:37,101 --> 00:45:38,703
Sang-eun?

698
00:45:38,769 --> 00:45:41,439
Oh! The girl who wants to be an idol?

699
00:45:41,505 --> 00:45:44,108
Why are you celebrating her birthday?

700
00:45:44,175 --> 00:45:46,410
That's none of your business.

701
00:45:47,111 --> 00:45:50,314
Right? None of my business. Sorry.

702
00:45:50,381 --> 00:45:52,450
-Oh, my sweet boy!
-Welcome home.

703
00:45:52,516 --> 00:45:54,552
How was the picnic? Was it fun?

704
00:45:54,619 --> 00:45:55,920
No.

705
00:45:55,987 --> 00:45:57,655
Why? Did you and a friend fight?

706
00:45:57,722 --> 00:45:59,390
No, I didn't.

707
00:45:59,457 --> 00:46:02,093
Um, is Min-gi still not home yet?

708
00:46:02,159 --> 00:46:04,528
Huh? No, he's not home yet.

709
00:46:20,511 --> 00:46:24,649
Dad, you're going to Seoul tomorrow
for the farmers' market, right?

710
00:46:24,715 --> 00:46:29,387
On your way back, for my birthday,
get me just one pair of headphones.

711
00:46:31,989 --> 00:46:34,692
Why not?
What's wrong with listening to music?

712
00:46:37,762 --> 00:46:39,664
You always say you're broke, jeez.

713
00:46:39,730 --> 00:46:41,465
Forget it. Never mind.

714
00:46:41,532 --> 00:46:43,567
I'm stupid for counting on you, ugh.

715
00:46:43,634 --> 00:46:45,236
This is so annoying, jeez!

716
00:46:54,211 --> 00:46:55,980
Damn it all to hell.

717
00:46:56,047 --> 00:46:58,416
I pick and pick, but rocks keep coming.

718
00:46:58,482 --> 00:47:00,318
Was this place an old quarry? Damn it!

719
00:47:00,918 --> 00:47:03,888
-Let's take a break, Boss.
-Ugh, damn. Let's do that.

720
00:47:06,023 --> 00:47:10,027
I'm really not cut out
for weekend farming, damn it.

721
00:47:10,094 --> 00:47:12,229
This is such pointless crap, this is.

722
00:47:21,405 --> 00:47:23,874
Wait, Boss, where are you going?

723
00:47:23,941 --> 00:47:25,843
Hey, I'll be right back.

724
00:47:25,910 --> 00:47:27,978
You all finish picking out the rocks.

725
00:47:31,215 --> 00:47:32,850
Excuse me.

726
00:47:39,357 --> 00:47:40,858
You're In-gi, right?

727
00:47:41,992 --> 00:47:43,394
You're Han In-gyu, right?

728
00:47:44,862 --> 00:47:46,564
Don't you recognize me?

729
00:47:48,666 --> 00:47:51,202
It's me, Seung-cheol.

730
00:47:56,307 --> 00:48:00,411
Where are you running, you bastard?
Don't we have a lot to talk about?

731
00:48:05,282 --> 00:48:08,853
What are you doing right now?
Are you mocking me?

732
00:48:14,091 --> 00:48:15,726
What's with this bastard?

733
00:48:16,293 --> 00:48:19,463
Hey, what's wrong with you? Huh?

734
00:48:20,898 --> 00:48:26,904
I'M SORRY

735
00:48:28,939 --> 00:48:33,344
Damn it, does "sorry" fix everything?

736
00:48:33,411 --> 00:48:36,614
Know what happened to us
after you vanished like that?

737
00:48:37,248 --> 00:48:40,651
Sang-pil drives a cab now,
and Geon-tae sells fruit on a truck.

738
00:48:41,786 --> 00:48:44,722
And I lend money to others
and live off the interest

739
00:48:44,789 --> 00:48:47,324
like a lowlife thug, you bastard!

740
00:48:50,995 --> 00:48:53,764
Hey, tell me.

741
00:48:53,831 --> 00:48:57,668
Why the hell did you vanish
without a word back then?

742
00:49:11,148 --> 00:49:12,716
If you ruined others' lives,

743
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:14,819
you could at least live in style.

744
00:49:14,885 --> 00:49:16,921
Look at this pathetic mess, damn it.

745
00:49:18,088 --> 00:49:19,890
Come on, tell me.

746
00:49:19,957 --> 00:49:23,427
Why on earth did you do that back then?

747
00:49:26,997 --> 00:49:29,934
Was it because of Suk-kyeong?

748
00:49:30,668 --> 00:49:32,102
PRACTICE IS HOW WE SURVIVE

749
00:49:32,169 --> 00:49:34,338
Okay, okay, okay! Is everyone ready?

750
00:49:34,405 --> 00:49:35,739
Yes, sir!

751
00:49:35,806 --> 00:49:37,875
You know Dream Records' CEO is coming?

752
00:49:37,942 --> 00:49:40,978
-The CEO, the CEO!
-Do well today, and we'll debut!

753
00:49:41,045 --> 00:49:43,180
-Debut!
-Debut, debut!

754
00:49:44,148 --> 00:49:46,317
Don't you worry one little bit, man.

755
00:49:46,383 --> 00:49:49,019
We've got In-gi, Mr. Popular himself!

756
00:49:49,086 --> 00:49:52,823
Once In-gi goes on, they're dead meat.

757
00:49:53,791 --> 00:49:55,392
In-gi, you can do this, right?

758
00:49:55,459 --> 00:49:57,695
Hey, don't worry.

759
00:49:57,761 --> 00:50:00,698
I'll put my life on the line
like it's our last shot.

760
00:50:00,764 --> 00:50:04,869
Let's finally make it big
and live proudly for all to see.

761
00:50:04,935 --> 00:50:07,905
No more eating dust
in a basement room every day.

762
00:50:07,972 --> 00:50:10,875
I'll only stop eating
that damn ramen when I die.

763
00:50:10,941 --> 00:50:13,244
Right, we're all counting on you.

764
00:50:13,310 --> 00:50:15,713
-Okay!
-In-gi's all we've got!

765
00:50:19,016 --> 00:50:21,118
Hello?

766
00:50:21,185 --> 00:50:22,419
Yes.

767
00:50:23,187 --> 00:50:24,922
One moment, please.

768
00:50:24,989 --> 00:50:26,624
In-gi, answer the phone.

769
00:50:31,362 --> 00:50:32,897
Hello?

770
00:50:32,963 --> 00:50:34,231
Yes.

771
00:50:35,065 --> 00:50:36,634
What did you say?

772
00:50:46,644 --> 00:50:48,312
Where are you going?

773
00:50:50,147 --> 00:50:53,017
They say Suk-kyeong collapsed.

774
00:50:54,985 --> 00:50:57,254
-I have to go.
-You bastard!

775
00:50:57,321 --> 00:50:58,956
Is now the time for that?

776
00:50:59,023 --> 00:51:02,159
If you leave now, it's all over. Over!

777
00:51:03,661 --> 00:51:05,062
I'm sorry.

778
00:51:07,164 --> 00:51:10,234
You bastard. Hey, In-gi! Han In-gi!

779
00:51:17,308 --> 00:51:19,276
Where's patient Yoon Suk-kyeong?

780
00:51:20,244 --> 00:51:22,880
Are you Yoon Suk-kyeong's family?

781
00:51:22,947 --> 00:51:25,282
-Yes.
-This way, please.

782
00:51:27,284 --> 00:51:31,055
Congratulations, Yoon Suk-kyeong.
You had a beautiful little princess.

783
00:51:41,131 --> 00:51:42,633
Honey.

784
00:51:43,801 --> 00:51:45,436
Are you okay?

785
00:51:49,640 --> 00:51:52,710
-Honey.
-You did so well, honey.

786
00:51:54,778 --> 00:51:56,380
What about your performance?

787
00:51:57,881 --> 00:52:01,352
-Would you like to hold the baby?
-What? Yes.

788
00:52:12,363 --> 00:52:15,299
She's bleeding heavily.
Check her blood pressure.

789
00:52:15,366 --> 00:52:17,868
Ma'am, are you okay? Ma'am?

790
00:52:17,935 --> 00:52:20,004
Her blood pressure keeps dropping.

791
00:52:20,070 --> 00:52:21,538
This is bad. Send him out.

792
00:52:21,605 --> 00:52:23,841
-Prep for surgery now.
-Give me the baby.

793
00:52:23,907 --> 00:52:25,442
Sir, please step outside.

794
00:52:25,509 --> 00:52:28,212
Suk-kyeong! Suk-kyeong!

795
00:52:28,278 --> 00:52:31,148
Suk-kyeong! No, Suk-kyeong!

796
00:52:31,215 --> 00:52:34,652
Suk-kyeong! Suk-kyeong!

797
00:52:35,519 --> 00:52:38,088
Suk-kyeong!

798
00:52:45,663 --> 00:52:48,065
Is that why you're a pathetic wreck?

799
00:52:48,132 --> 00:52:50,367
You ruined your friends' lives for that

800
00:52:50,434 --> 00:52:53,904
and holed up in this rural backwater,
you bastard?

801
00:53:03,514 --> 00:53:06,083
I'M SORRY

802
00:53:12,990 --> 00:53:15,292
SUK-KYEONG DIED BECAUSE OF ME

803
00:53:16,860 --> 00:53:18,295
How's that because of you?

804
00:53:18,362 --> 00:53:20,330
Your wife died having a baby,

805
00:53:20,397 --> 00:53:22,132
so how's that your fault, you bastard?

806
00:53:49,760 --> 00:53:52,329
Where do I dig for nothing today?

807
00:53:54,331 --> 00:53:56,633
I paint by day and dig by night.

808
00:53:56,700 --> 00:53:59,937
I'll work myself to death
before I find the money, jeez.

809
00:54:05,776 --> 00:54:07,244
INCOMING CALL: MADAM

810
00:54:09,580 --> 00:54:12,883
Hello? I told you not to call me.

811
00:54:15,185 --> 00:54:18,055
Did those thugs come by again?

812
00:54:18,122 --> 00:54:19,423
Don't get me started.

813
00:54:19,490 --> 00:54:23,694
They come by all the time,
raising hell to make me rat you out.

814
00:54:24,361 --> 00:54:27,931
You're going through all that
because of me… I'm real sorry.

815
00:54:27,998 --> 00:54:31,568
But seriously, where are you?

816
00:54:32,703 --> 00:54:36,140
Uh, well… I'll explain later. Later.

817
00:54:36,206 --> 00:54:38,375
Okay, you little brat.

818
00:54:38,442 --> 00:54:41,178
Anyway, take care of yourself.

819
00:54:41,245 --> 00:54:43,380
And call me if anything happens.

820
00:54:43,447 --> 00:54:46,717
-Okay?
-Sure, got it.

821
00:55:03,300 --> 00:55:05,369
SUCCESS

822
00:55:28,158 --> 00:55:31,528
Forget it. You don't need to explain.

823
00:55:34,665 --> 00:55:36,533
Now that I think about it…

824
00:55:37,634 --> 00:55:39,436
it all makes sense now.

825
00:55:40,237 --> 00:55:43,907
You never talked about Mom until now,

826
00:55:45,342 --> 00:55:48,612
and my whole life, you never once
bought me a birthday cake.

827
00:55:50,347 --> 00:55:52,049
It's because my birthday…

828
00:55:54,651 --> 00:55:56,854
is Mom's death anniversary, isn't it?

829
00:56:04,228 --> 00:56:06,597
It was all because of me.

830
00:56:07,297 --> 00:56:09,900
If only I hadn't been born,

831
00:56:09,967 --> 00:56:11,535
Mom wouldn't have died,

832
00:56:12,236 --> 00:56:14,872
and you wouldn't be like this.

833
00:56:14,938 --> 00:56:17,374
I'm so sorry, Dad.

834
00:56:25,883 --> 00:56:27,117
Let go!

835
00:56:27,184 --> 00:56:29,820
I don't want to talk to you right now.

836
00:56:35,893 --> 00:56:38,896
Sang-eun! S-Sang-eun!

837
00:56:44,201 --> 00:56:47,004
Sang-eun, no!

838
00:57:16,633 --> 00:57:18,201
Mom?

839
00:57:31,081 --> 00:57:33,984
Why come out in your condition?
Go inside and rest.

840
00:57:34,051 --> 00:57:35,986
I'm doing just fine.

841
00:57:36,053 --> 00:57:38,889
Today's an important show, isn't it?

842
00:57:38,956 --> 00:57:43,160
An agency CEO interested in our band
is supposed to come in person.

843
00:57:43,226 --> 00:57:46,063
If things go well…
we might get to release an album.

844
00:57:46,697 --> 00:57:48,065
That's wonderful!

845
00:57:48,131 --> 00:57:50,334
Do well today. You've got this!

846
00:57:51,335 --> 00:57:52,636
Um…

847
00:57:53,337 --> 00:57:56,540
If it doesn't work out this time,
I'll quit music for good.

848
00:57:56,606 --> 00:57:58,342
Bear with me a little longer.

849
00:57:59,076 --> 00:58:01,078
Please don't talk like that.

850
00:58:01,144 --> 00:58:04,281
I believe in you, dear,
so you must never give up.

851
00:58:04,348 --> 00:58:06,984
-Got it?
-Okay, thanks.

852
00:58:07,050 --> 00:58:08,986
I'm heading out now.

853
00:58:10,354 --> 00:58:11,989
Um, wait a moment.

854
00:58:20,030 --> 00:58:21,765
Forget it, I don't need money.

855
00:58:23,033 --> 00:58:25,802
A man can't go out with empty pockets.

856
00:58:28,972 --> 00:58:31,842
If it goes well,
go grab a drink with the band.

857
00:58:34,511 --> 00:58:37,347
I'm sorry I make life so hard for you.

858
00:58:38,215 --> 00:58:40,851
I'm too ashamed to face you.

859
00:58:40,917 --> 00:58:44,388
It's not hard at all. Hurry on now.

860
00:58:44,454 --> 00:58:45,422
Go on, honey.

861
00:58:45,489 --> 00:58:48,358
-All right, I'll be back.
-Okay, off you go.

862
00:58:48,425 --> 00:58:50,460
-Okay.
-Do great today! Go for it!

863
00:58:50,527 --> 00:58:52,763
-See you later.
-Shoulders back, honey.

864
00:58:52,829 --> 00:58:55,065
-Sure.
-Your hair! Fix your hair!

865
00:59:13,450 --> 00:59:15,519
I'm back, ma'am.

866
00:59:15,585 --> 00:59:19,790
Does your husband have no conscience?

867
00:59:19,856 --> 00:59:22,325
How can he make a woman
who's due any day now

868
00:59:22,392 --> 00:59:24,127
go out and earn money?

869
00:59:26,396 --> 00:59:28,432
Please don't say that.

870
00:59:28,498 --> 00:59:30,333
Soon enough, my husband

871
00:59:30,400 --> 00:59:33,970
will be even more famous
than Cho Yong-pil.

872
00:59:34,604 --> 00:59:36,973
Cho Yong-pil? In your dreams.

873
00:59:37,040 --> 00:59:39,509
That two-bit musician
can't even pay the bills…

874
00:59:39,576 --> 00:59:41,711
Please don't talk like that.

875
00:59:41,778 --> 00:59:43,180
My baby will hear you.

876
00:59:43,246 --> 00:59:46,983
It's not true. Your dad's a great man.

877
00:59:48,385 --> 00:59:51,021
I'll finish cleaning this up.

878
00:59:51,088 --> 00:59:53,490
-Okay, put those in the back.
-Yes, ma'am.

879
01:00:01,765 --> 01:00:03,133
Oh, no! Honey!

880
01:00:16,813 --> 01:00:18,181
It's all…

881
01:00:19,349 --> 01:00:22,686
it's all my fault.

882
01:00:24,087 --> 01:00:28,492
I just had to pursue music.

883
01:00:29,159 --> 01:00:30,694
If only…

884
01:00:30,760 --> 01:00:34,297
if only I hadn't been so stubborn.

885
01:00:40,737 --> 01:00:43,473
Your mom…

886
01:00:43,540 --> 01:00:45,942
I… I…

887
01:00:46,610 --> 01:00:49,012
I killed her.

888
01:00:49,079 --> 01:00:51,014
That's not true!

889
01:00:51,882 --> 01:00:54,584
Dad, it's not your fault.

890
01:00:57,821 --> 01:00:59,189
I…

891
01:01:05,195 --> 01:01:07,164
Hey, hey, be gentle with those.

892
01:01:07,230 --> 01:01:10,200
We can't sell bruised ones
at tomorrow's farmers market.

893
01:01:10,267 --> 01:01:11,168
Got it.

894
01:01:11,234 --> 01:01:13,670
-Like a baby…
-Mom, when is Min-gi coming?

895
01:01:13,737 --> 01:01:15,105
Can't you call him?

896
01:01:15,172 --> 01:01:17,340
He'll get here when he gets here.

897
01:01:17,407 --> 01:01:19,743
Min-ho, it's cold. Go inside.

898
01:01:19,809 --> 01:01:20,944
I don't want to.

899
01:01:21,011 --> 01:01:23,180
I'll wait until Min-gi gets here.

900
01:01:31,054 --> 01:01:33,857
It's Min-gi! Min-gi!

901
01:01:41,831 --> 01:01:43,400
Hey!

902
01:01:53,643 --> 01:01:54,811
It's Y-Yu-na!
